% Fabric words: the tariff's own definitions, and US Customs rulings
"jersey" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric".
"interlock" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric".
"rib" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in ruling NY N352158, confer "rib knit fabric for the neckband".
"broadcloth" is a fabric of construction woven,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "The term \"poplin or broadcloth\" means plain weave fabrics".
"poplin" is a fabric of construction woven,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "The term \"poplin or broadcloth\" means plain weave fabrics".
"denim" is a fabric of construction woven,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 52, confer "the expression \"denim\" means fabrics of yarns of different colors".


